# GitHub-hosted builds

Status: all four ordinary hosted product builds qualified in separate clean
runs; signing authority and dependency-cache qualification remain pending.

## Scope

Move build-only work to disposable GitHub-hosted runners, retaining the existing
build/package scripts and all dependency-patch, version, closure and privacy
gates. No product deployments, runtime changes, hardware-test replacement,
automatic release publication or paid larger-runner provisioning.

Build Linux Host inside pinned Rocky Linux 9.7 on a Linux runner; Linux Client
on Ubuntu 26.04; native Host and Client on arm64 macOS27/SDK27. The current
GitHub `xcode-27` preview runs macOS27; assert actual OS/SDK before building.
Keep CUDA architecture coverage unchanged. Size concurrency to runner resources.

The separate private infrastructure repositories own their own Ubuntu26.04
workflows. They are not inputs to this public workflow. Never put deployment
inventory, account information, credentials or private source into public CI.

## Implementation order

1. Private standalone Ubuntu package workflows: existing tests and package
   gates, clean worktrees, explicit branch versions, private artifact retention.
2. Public clean-worktree bootstrap and four product jobs. Pin Actions by SHA;
   use read-only tokens and persist-credentials=false. No SSH to local machines.
3. Verify real hosted runs; resolve toolchain/setup failures without weakening
   product gates. Cache pinned prepared inputs, not dirty product builds.
   Cache misses must reproduce dependencies and patches from source.
4. Add separately protected macOS distribution signing when the operator
   provisions Developer ID and notarization credentials. PR jobs never get
   secrets; no pull_request_target or untrusted workflow_run execution.
5. Independently qualify signed packages, then decide whether local build-only
   VMs can be retired. Keep physical Linux/macOS test machines.

## Validation

Test branch/ref handling, clean worktrees, exact pins and secret boundaries.
Run the actual hosted jobs and retain links, conclusions and artifact hashes.
Unsigned Mac developer builds are not distributable packages. Missing signing
credentials and missing private cross-repository integration credentials must
be reported explicitly, never described as passed validation.

Runner/container updates can change tools; assert required versions, record
installed package versions and SDKs. No unbounded cache retention, guessed
dependency fallbacks, disabled privacy gates or reduced CUDA targets.

References:
- https://docs.github.com/en/actions/reference/runners/github-hosted-runners
- https://github.blog/changelog/2026-09-10-xcode-27-runner-image-now-runs-on-macos-27/
- https://docs.github.com/en/actions/how-tos/write-workflows/choose-where-workflows-run/run-jobs-in-a-container
